{{!--
  Trick hero block: breadcrumbs, the h1, and a subtitle. Nothing else.

  It carries no structural decomposition strip and no ADD formula. For a
  trick whose name is its decomposition, as many are, the two of them would
  restate the h1 twice over: "Ducking Toe Stall", then `ducking` `toe stall`,
  then `ducking(+1) + toe stall`. The decomposition sits below the
  plain-words opening, where it belongs, and only the formula is kept of the
  two because it carries the arithmetic the strip would leave implicit.

  Sparse pages with no summary fall back to the records-side sortname for
  identity continuity, unless it only repeats the h1. The hashtag is not a
  hero part: it renders in the media line at the top of the page body, and
  the taxonomy chips (family, ADD, pronunciation) render in the body too.
--}}
<div class="hero hero-sm">
  <div>
    {{#if navigation.breadcrumbs}}
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      {{#each navigation.breadcrumbs}}
        {{#if href}}<a href="{{href}}">{{label}}</a> <span class="breadcrumb-sep">/</span> {{else}}<span>{{label}}</span>{{/if}}
      {{/each}}
    </nav>
    {{/if}}
    <h1>{{page.title}}</h1>
    {{#if summary}}
    <p class="hero-subtitle">{{summary}}</p>
    {{else}}
      {{#if content.sortName}}<p class="hero-subtitle">{{content.sortName}}</p>{{/if}}
    {{/if}}
  </div>
</div>
